Hokku's window frames round other apps' windows

With window.decorator: Haiku (or Gonx) in the theme, labwc draws Hokku's own
frame round every window it decorates (Wayland and X11 apps) instead of its
titlebar and border: Haiku's yellow tab with the close and zoom boxes, or
Gonx's. The frame is painted by Hokku's frame code (gonx-frame.c and
haiku-frame.c, which the PKGBUILD copies into src/ssd/hokku/) and hit-tested
with it, so the tab moves the window, its buttons close, zoom and minimize,
and the border resizes, as on Hokku's own windows.

window.decorator.font sets the title font (a Pango description such as
"Noto Sans Bold 12px"); without it, rc.xml's ActiveWindow font is used.
The tab colours are window.*.title.bg.color, the title window.*.label.text.color
and Haiku's border window.*.border.color.

